@@ -48,3 +48,29 @@ Deck is clean. No production code exists in `js/` yet.
 **Verification:** Scenario fails red as expected -- `Given the root index.html exists at the project root` asserts file existence and the file is absent. Dry-run: 31 scenarios, 125 steps, all parsable.
 
 **Handoff to QM:** Red target is `features/root-index-html.feature:Root index.html exists with correct structure and script`. Crew must create a root `index.html` built from `assets/app-template.index.html` that loads `js/app.js` via a script tag. The scenario will go green when the file exists with the correct structure.
+
+### Voyage: Browser acceptance suite defect triage
+
+**Problem:** An external Cypress acceptance suite runs against the built app in a real browser. The in-harness suite (happy-dom) passes all 31 scenarios, but the browser suite reports 6 failures. These are real product defects invisible to the in-harness DOM.
+
+**Root causes identified:**
+
+1. **DOM node replacement on state change** (Cypress failures 1-4): `render()` in `app.js` calls `todoList.innerHTML = ''` and recreates every `<li>` from scratch. When Cypress clicks a checkbox, the click handler calls `toggleTodo()` which calls `render()`, destroying all DOM nodes. Cypress holds a stale reference and throws `element-has-detached-from-dom`. The in-harness suite does not catch this because its step definitions call `findTodoByTitle()` after every action, re-querying the DOM.
+
+2. **Toggle control visible during editing** (Cypress failure 5): The acceptance test asserts the `.toggle` input is hidden when editing mode is active. The current app does not hide the toggle control during editing. The in-harness suite does not check CSS display state on the toggle during editing.
+
+3. **Copy-paste error in filter link class** (Cypress failure 6): Line 104 of `app.js` reads `link.classList.add('completed')` instead of `link.classList.add('selected')`. The Completed filter link gets class `completed` instead of `selected` when `#/completed` is active.
+
+**Specs authored:**
+
+| New spec | Scenario | Pins |
+|---|---|---|
+| `features/dom-stability.feature` | Toggling a todo preserves DOM node identity | DOM nodes must remain attached across toggle |
+| `features/dom-stability.feature` | Toggle all preserves DOM node identity for each item | DOM nodes must remain attached across toggle-all |
+| `features/dom-stability.feature` | Clearing completed preserves DOM node identity for remaining items | DOM nodes must remain attached across clear-completed |
+| `features/editing.feature:47` | Toggle control is hidden when editing | `.toggle` input must have `display: none` when `li.editing` |
+| `features/routing.feature:31` | Completed filter link has selected class | Completed link must get class `selected` |
+
+**Verification:** All 5 new scenarios fail red against current code. All 31 original scenarios pass. 32 pass, 5 fail total.
+
+**Handoff to QM:** Three product defects, five red targets. DOM stability requires incremental DOM updates in `app.js` — mutate existing nodes in place instead of rebuilding the list. Editing visibility requires hiding the `.toggle` input when the `li` has class `editing`. Filter class requires fixing line 104: `completed` → `selected`.
