@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+Feature: DOM stability during state changes
+  As a TodoMVC user
+  I want the app to update todo items in place when their state changes
+  So that the interface feels responsive and browser-held element references remain valid
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves its DOM node identity
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    When I click the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then todo "Buy milk" has class "completed"
+    And the DOM node for todo "Buy milk" is the same element as before the click
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all preserves DOM node identity for each item
+    Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When I check the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos are marked complete
+    And the DOM node for todo "Buy milk" is the same element as before the click
+    And the DOM node for todo "Walk dog" is the same element as before the click
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed preserves DOM node identity for remaining items
+    Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And I mark todo "Buy milk" as complete
+    When I click the clear completed button
+    Then todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+    And todo "Walk dog" is visible
+    And the DOM node for todo "Walk dog" is the same element as before the click
